      "final_text": "我们的观点：投资者目前聚焦于长端收益率急剧上行的原因。短端收益率（约5年期以内）通常主要受经济数据、美联储预期及周期性背景等基本面因素驱动，而5年期以上（尤其是接近30年期）的收益率则受期限溢价及与近期美联储定价关联不紧密的力量所主导。这些因素包括供需动态、财政预测、政治与地缘政治风险，以及全球久期溢出效应。地缘政治不确定性、大规模人工智能(AI)相关债务发行，以及日本长端利率产生的压力，是当前导致长端收益率居高不下或波动加剧的因素。叠加财政赤字持续扩大，我们认为期限溢价在短期内不会出现明显下行趋势。另一个理解长端压力的视角是买方结构的变化——随着主要买家由对价格不敏感的境外机构转向对价格敏感的私人投资者，投资者要求更高的收益率。尽管如此，若出现全面经济衰退，整条收益率曲线可能均会下行。尽管近期经济疲软态势或将延续，但全面经济衰退不是我们的基准情景。对于风险偏好较低的投资者而言，5年期以上的长期美国国债可作为应对下行尾部风险的对冲工具——我们认为未来12至18个月内发生全面经济衰退的概率约为25%。",
      "iterations": 0,
      "seg_status": "edited",
      "source_text": "What we think Investors have focused on why yields on the long-end moving sharply higher. While the short end (up to ~5Y) tends to be dominated by fundamentals such as economic data, Fed expectations, and the cyclical backdrop, yields beyond 5Y (and especially close to 30Y) are driven by term premium and forces that don’t map cleanly to near-term Fed pricing. These include factors such as supply-demand dynamics, fiscal projections, political and geopolitical risk, and global duration spillovers. Geopolitical uncertainty, heavy AI-related debt issuance, and Japan’s long-end pressures are current examples of forces that can keep the long end elevated or volatile. Combined with expanding fiscal deficits, we don’t see term premium trending meaningfully downward anytime soon. Another way to think about the pressures on the long-end is the changing composition of buyers – as the primary buyer shifts towards price-sensitive private investors (instead of price insensitive foreign institutions), investors are demanding a higher yield. That being said, a full-on recessionary scenario would likely pull down the entire curve. While the recent stretch of economic softness may continue, a full recession is not our base case. For the more risk-averse investor, longer-dated Treasuries beyond 5Y can make sense as a hedge to that downside tail risk – we assign roughly ~25% odds of a full recession over the next 12–18 months.",
